WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.930
Hollywood once had a habit of handling superhero
properties poorly, and 1997's Spawn remains

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.380
a prime example of that.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.480
Creator Todd McFarlane knows that the first
adaptation was a missed opportunity, which

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.150
is exactly why he's going to make certain
the reboot blows you away.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:15.640
How?

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.280
Here's a look.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.100
McFarlane was something of a superhero himself
in the late '80s and early '90s, at least

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.169
in comic book circles.

00:00:22.169 --> 00:00:27.009
He rose to prominence with his hugely successful
run on The Amazing Spider-Man, co-creating

00:00:27.009 --> 00:00:28.880
the anti-hero Venom along the way.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.240
Even Stan Lee was amazed at his abilities.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.640
"We'll try to explain our thinking on how
we're coming across, and why we're doing Overkill

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.140
the way…"

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.580
"You can think and draw at the same time?!"

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.960
Given Venom's massive box office success,
it's no surprise than McFarlane sees possibilities

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.500
for the similarly horror-tinged Spawn.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:49.850
Where Venom opted for a more family friendly
PG-13 rating, though, McFarlane promises to

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.039
push the envelope with a truly R-rated superhero
movie.

00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:56.870
During an appearance at ACE Comic Con in 2018,
McFarlane said,

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:59.239
"We don't want to muddy the waters, it's R-rated.

00:00:59.239 --> 00:01:02.600
Not like Deadpool, where there was just a
couple F-bombs and a naked butt.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.780
Not like Logan either…

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.640
We're talking trauma, true trauma, as serious
as possible."

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:11.530
McFarlane even holds out hope that Sony may
choose to distribute the new Spawn film, leading

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:14.480
to a potential crossover between his two creations.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:15.480
He told CBR,

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.500
"No matter who distributes Spawn, the first
thing you will see in every trailer will be,

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.740
'From the co-creator of Venom.'

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:25.720
So then my question to Sony is, why would
you let one of your competitors use that line,

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.670
given that it was your effort that made Venom
work?...

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:30.500
I think it's worth asking, then, what happens
if they both work?"

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.980
Of course, we already know what will happen
if it doesn't work.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:37.200
"You will be this legless, armless, faceless
thing, won't you?

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.660
Rolling down the street, like a turd in the
wind."

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.780
Where Venom just had undertones of horror,
though, McFarlane promises Spawn will be pure

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:47.380
terror.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:52.480
In fact, he told Deadline that his dedication
to a truly dark Spawn film has led to difficulties

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:54.860
with Hollywood execs who don't understand
his vision.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:59.260
"They all default into their Captain America
mindset and I keep saying, 'No, get into John

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:01.240
Carpenter's mindset or Hitchcock.'

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:05.360
This is not a man in a rubber suit, it's not
a hero that's going to come and save the damsel,

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:05.860
it's none of that."

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.400
One way he plans to do this is by abandoning
the tired superhero cliche of presenting an

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:11.460
origin film.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.780
McFarlane told ComicBook.com he plans to just
jump right into the action instead.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.700
"I've seen too many movies that spend way
too much time for the set up."

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.700
One way McFarlane is working to deliver on
his many promises is by surrounding himself

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:24.880
with top notch talent.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.600
Producer Jason Blum, who was behind the massive
hit Split, is on board, while superstars Jamie

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.310
Foxx and Jeremy Renner are slated to play
the leads.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:33.520
Yes, leads, plural.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:37.700
That's because Foxx's portrayal of Spawn will
largely be in a supporting role.

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:41.770
Instead, Renner's brainy cop Twitch will be
at the center of the story, as he seeks revenge

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:45.840
for the death of his daughter while the specter
of the bogeyman Spawn looms in the shadows.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.220
Foxx told Yahoo! that he's sure the final
result will be epic.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:53.140
"Todd McFarlane is already a badass, but then
you see Jeremy Renner, and you go, 'Wow.'

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:56.830
Because the script revolves around the character
Twitch, and you can look at Jeremy Renner's

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:58.900
face for an hour and a half and be moved.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.580
That's a wonderful partner, and it makes you
feel good about the project."

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:06.420
After what happened the first time he allowed
somebody else to adapt his prized property,

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.760
McFarlane understandably wanted a higher degree
of control this time out.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:14.520
In fact, what the Spawn creator has is essentially
full control; He's writing and directing the

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:15.180
movie himself.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:19.740
That allows him to go outside the studio system,
where execs are more concerned with moving

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:20.960
tie-in merchandise.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:23.740
McFarlane told fans at New York Comic Con
2018,

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.530
"I don't care about selling t-shirts and hats.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:29.209
When Spawn comes, it's nice and calm, and
then you're gone.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.680
He will mess you up and he will do it in a
harsh way.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.200
He doesn't care if he's selling any toys or
t-shirts."

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:39.720
These days many superhero blockbusters routinely
cost hundreds of millions of dollars to make.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:43.940
But the new Spawn reboot is reportedly only
going to cost $10 million, which is just a

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:47.020
quarter of that the original cost way back
in 1997.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:47.780
How?

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:51.880
According to Blum, neither he nor McFarlane
are taking any pay from the budget, and neither

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:52.380
are the stars.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:56.980
Plus, they are creating a much smaller, more
contained world, filled with practical effects

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.280
rather than CGI.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:02.340
As part of that, McFarlane hired emmy award
winning Walking Dead director and special

00:04:02.349 --> 00:04:07.130
effects guru Greg Nicotero to design the world
of Spawn, including a new costume that is

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:08.780
streamlined for movie audiences.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:10.380
McFarlane revealed to Fandom,

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.340
"We've already designed them, and the great
thing about Greg is, because he's a director,

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:18.280
when I was trying to explain what I was going
to do onscreen visually he could understand

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:19.280
what that meant."

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:23.479
Netflix has had its ups and downs when it
comes to original movies, with hits like Bird

00:04:23.479 --> 00:04:26.380
Box and flops like the manga adaptation Death
Note.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:30.919
Either way, McFarlane told Comicbook.com he
may consider distributing Spawn through Netflix.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:34.699
"I think the world's changing in front of
our very eyes in how we're going to consume

00:04:34.699 --> 00:04:36.750
not only entertainment, but even movies…

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:41.460
I'm not going to get married to a distribution
model that may not be as relevant or as efficient

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.059
because that's how you used to do it.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.120
I'll talk to all of them."

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:48.180
If you like the sound of all this, well, you're
in luck, because McFarlane told the crowd

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:51.580
at New York Comic Con that he's actually planning
a whole Spawn trilogy.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.659
"I'm selling it as a trilogy, and each movie
will look different than the last one.

00:04:55.659 --> 00:04:59.639
Here's the thing about the trilogy: A lot
of trilogies go back and repeat the last thing.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.620
I want each movie to be visually different."

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:04.200
So why a trilogy instead of a stand alone
film?

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:07.180
"Why do you people always question?

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:08.440
Why ask why?

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.940
When how is so much more fun!"

